st_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…And if ye walk contrary unto me, and will not hearken unto me; I will bring seven times more plagues upon you according to your sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨I will also send wild beasts among you, which shall rob you of your children, and destroy your cattle, and make you few in number; and your high ways shall be desolate.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd if ye will not be reformed by me by these things, but will walk contrary unto me;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[then will I also walk contrary unto you, and will punish you yet seven times for your sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙâAnd I will bring a sword upon you, that shall avenge the quarrel of my covenant: and when ye are gathered together within your cities, I will send the pestilence among you; and ye shall be delivered into the hand of the enemy.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»And when I have broken the staff of your bread, ten women shall bake your bread in one oven, and they shall deliver you your bread again by weight: and ye shall eat, and not be satisfied.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse'¦verses„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKAnd if ye will not for all this hearken unto me, but walk contrary unto me;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlthen I will walk contrary unto you also in fury; and I, even I, will chastise you seven times for your sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd ye shall eat the flesh of your sons, and the flesh of your daughters shall ye eat.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“And I will destroy your high places, and cut down your images, and cast your carcases upon the carcases of your idols, and my soul shall abhor you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And I will make your cities waste, and bring your sanctuaries unto desolation, and I will not smell the savour of your sweet odours.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd I will bring the land into desolation: and your enemies which dwell therein shall be astonished at it.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And I will scatter you among the heathen, and will draw out a sword after you: and your land shall be desolate, and your cities waste.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen shall the land enjoy her sabbaths, as long as it lieth desolate, and ye be in your enemies' land; even then shall the land rest, and enjoy her sabbaths.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlAs long as it lieth desolate it shall rest; because it did not rest in your sabbaths, when ye dwelt upon it.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙøAnd upon them that are left alive of you I will send a faintness into their hearts in the lands of their enemies; and the sound of a shaken leaf shall chase them; and they shall flee, as fleeing from a sword; and they shall fall when none pursueth.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd they shall fall one upon another, as it were before a sword, when none pursueth: and ye shall have no power to stand before your enemies.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd ye shall perish among the heathen, and the land of your enemies shall eat you up.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£And they that are left of you shall pine away in their iniquity in your enemies' lands; and also in the iniquities of their fathers shall they pine away with them.¦layout ªlast_verse'…¤book§chapter«first_verse(ªlast_verse-¦verses–„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯If they shall confess their iniquity, and the iniquity of their fathers, with their trespass which they trespassed against me, and that also they have walked contrary unto me;¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎand that I also have walked contrary unto them, and have brought them into the land of their enemies; if then their uncircumcised hearts be humbled, and they then accept of the punishment of their iniquity:¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙthen will I remember my covenant with Jacob, and also my covenant with Isaac, and also my covenant with Abraham will I remember; and I will remember the land.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚThe land also shall be left of them, and shall enjoy her sabbaths, while she lieth desolate without them: and they shall accept of the punishment of their iniquity: because, even because they despised my judgments, and because their soul abhorred my statutes.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙĞAnd yet for all that, when they be in the land of their enemies, I will not cast them away, neither will I abhor them, to destroy them utterly, and to break my covenant with them: for I am the LORD their God.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹But I will for their sakes remember the covenant of their ancestors, whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt in the sight of the heathen, that I might be their God: I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse-…¤book§chapter«first_verse.ªlast_verse.¦verses‘„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThese are the statutes and judgments and laws, which the LORD made between him and the children of Israel in mount Sinai by the hand of Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse.